+Show Application Configuration
+-------------------------------
+
+The ``config`` command displays the configuration values loaded by the
+Flask application as formatted JSON. It requires an application to be
+specified using the ``--app`` option. ::
+
+    $ flask --app hello config
+    {
+      "DEBUG": false,
+      "TESTING": false,
+      "SECRET_KEY": "***",
+      "APPLICATION_ROOT": "/"
+    }
+
+Use the ``--sort-keys`` option to sort the configuration keys alphabetically. ::
+
+    $ flask --app hello config --sort-keys
+    {
+      "APPLICATION_ROOT": "/",
+      "DEBUG": false,
+      "SECRET_KEY": "***",
+      "TESTING": false
+    }
+
+Configuration keys containing ``SECRET``, ``PASSWORD``, ``TOKEN``, or
+``KEY`` are masked with ``***`` to avoid exposing sensitive values in
+the command output. Matching is case-insensitive.
